    "updated_at": "2023-02-24T07:39:44Z",
    "body": "@annevk I guess @bkardell would know better the details, but the rule of thumb is that MathML tries to align on HTML so we probably want the HTML definition for MathML. And currently, it's only used in one place for attributes that exist in HTML (from GlobalEventHandlers and HTMLOrForeignElement), so only the top-level definition: https://w3c.github.io/mathml-core/#dom-and-javascript",
